 in south africa what are the  biggest barriers to making sure people  do have access to those tools  yeah and i think it's similarly i mean  even earlier in the pandemic we  experience a lot of you know shortages  when it comes to um accessing these  medical  tools like testing testing tools so and  as you know that we also  recently  encountered expert burns bans or other  travel bans which has unfortunately is  also kind of affecting even operations  we we are anticipating to get you know  testing um tools from other um parts of  the world however due to the current um  bans on you know south africa that in  itself affects our ability to actually  receive those those those testing uh  material to be able to um test um  patients in our in our operations so  unfortunately you know those are the  kind of um uh uh  sort of challenges that we that were  encountered much more broadly that um  countries have also imposed um export  bans and that's why um we are calling  for um you know sharing and  collaboration to enable um countries  like south africa with you know and that  they don't need to actually rely on  other countries um to be able to have  these testing we do have the  manufacturing capacity what is needed is  for for the technology to be shared so  that we can manufacture and be able to  better respond um to the demand in our  own countries without having to rely to  other um countries who have um  unfortunately imposed these um  restrictions okay so a call for more  sharing and what is ultimately a global  struggle a candidacy homo we're going to  leave it there thank you so much for  joining us on the show  thank you thank you so much for having  me

